{"authored" [{"question" "q-104055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =x+C \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =-x-C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-0-C \\\\ 0 & =0-C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2y=-2x+1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=x+1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=-2x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\sqrt{y}$\nthat satisfies the condition $y(1)=9.$  Assume that $y>0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & =2{x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2} \\\\ y & ={({x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $y>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+C)^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=9$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =((1)^{2}+C)^{2} \\\\ 9 & =(1+C)^{2} \\\\ 3 & =1+C \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+2)^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x^2+2)^2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ C-1 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(\\frac{5}{4}-e^{-x})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =5x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm {e}^{5x+C} \\\\  & =\\pm {e}^{C}{e}^{5x} \\\\  & =K{e}^{5x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3 \\\\ K{e}^{5\\cdot 0} & =3 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x}  \\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that  $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0.$ Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "a5f3e5f03f387c5a545cbc855fc0d68f5d920decc385e2d02bac45f56f99b312" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C.$\n\nNow let's apply the condition $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$ to find $C_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =0+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)   =  \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "a5f3e5f03f387c5a545cbc855fc0d68f5d920decc385e2d02bac45f56f99b312" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(-1)=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d2448865aca91aecc19a4b1a66aa5a815bfc865917ae71a92e878d7e28c7c0" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{1}{x}+x+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(-1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{1-(-1)^{2}-C(-1)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{C} & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d2448865aca91aecc19a4b1a66aa5a815bfc865917ae71a92e878d7e28c7c0" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94228d1cf50b4ffe133be171eee2ad6084302ecd52a10d818f64b11428885957" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" 