_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f453a8267dda6772768fb5cc64ac599b02883620473cd19645b4409abff5842a" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}+2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f453a8267dda6772768fb5cc64ac599b02883620473cd19645b4409abff5842a" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f453a8267dda6772768fb5cc64ac599b02883620473cd19645b4409abff5842a" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =5x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm {e}^{5x+C} \\\\  & =\\pm {e}^{C}{e}^{5x} \\\\  & =K{e}^{5x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3 \\\\ K{e}^{5\\cdot 0} & =3 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x}  \\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that  $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0.$ Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "a5f3e5f03f387c5a545cbc855fc0d68f5d920decc385e2d02bac45f56f99b312" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C.$\n\nNow let's apply the condition $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$ to find $C_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =0+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)   =  \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "a5f3e5f03f387c5a545cbc855fc0d68f5d920decc385e2d02bac45f56f99b312" "basis" 1262 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-104055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =x+C \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =-x-C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-0-C \\\\ 0 & =0-C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "419bff3195711dba4c75f08f3c1717b4688a5cc9704c9527092dd16761cd9b19"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2y=-2x+1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=x+1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=-2x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\sqrt{y}$\nthat satisfies the condition $y(1)=9.$  Assume that $y>0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & =2{x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2} \\\\ y & ={({x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $y>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+C)^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=9$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =((1)^{2}+C)^{2} \\\\ 9 & =(1+C)^{2} \\\\ 3 & =1+C \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+2)^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "419bff3195711dba4c75f08f3c1717b4688a5cc9704c9527092dd16761cd9b19"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x^2+2)^2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=xy$  that satisfies $y(0)=1.$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/2+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/2+C}\\, \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{{x}^{2}/2+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=1$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =K{e}^{0} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=xy$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{{x}^{2}/2}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "419bff3195711dba4c75f08f3c1717b4688a5cc9704c9527092dd16761cd9b19"} {"question" "q-355562" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355562" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{x^2/2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}=0$  that satisfies $y(1)=e.$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{-1/x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-1/x+C}\\, \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-1/x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{-1/x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=e$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e & =K{e}^{-1} \\\\ K & ={e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}=0$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=e$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{2-1/x}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "419bff3195711dba4c75f08f3c1717b4688a5cc9704c9527092dd16761cd9b19"} {"question" "q-355578" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355578" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{2-1/x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-14312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{-x}$ that satisfies $y(0)={e}^{-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-14312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,dx & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{e}^{-x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{-{e}^{-x}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{e}^{-x}+C} \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{-{e}^{-x}+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{-{e}^{-x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)={e}^{-1}$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-1} & =K{e}^{-{e}^{-0}} \\\\ {e}^{-1} & =K{e}^{-1} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{-x}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)={e}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-{e}^{-x}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-14312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "419bff3195711dba4c75f08f3c1717b4688a5cc9704c9527092dd16761cd9b19"} {"question" "q-14312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-14312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y={e}^{-1+x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-1+{e}^{-x}}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-1-{e}^{x}}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-{e}^{-x}}"] ["math" "y={e}^{{e}^{x}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-14312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{-{e}^{-x}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ that satisfies $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}.$ Assume that $0<x<\\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+8x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x+8\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x+4{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the right-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nwhere $C={C}_{1}+{C}_{2}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})+4{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+C & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡1+{\\pi }^{2}+C & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ that satisfies the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "419bff3195711dba4c75f08f3c1717b4688a5cc9704c9527092dd16761cd9b19"} {"question" "q-104065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4{x}^{2}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8{x}^{2}-{\\pi }^{2}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+8{x}^{2}-{\\pi }^{2}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4{x}^{2}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-79373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies $y(1)=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-79373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y} & =4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}-{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(4{x}^{3}-1){e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3}-1 \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4{x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (4{x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{4}-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{4}-1+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡C & =0 \\\\ C & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-79373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "419bff3195711dba4c75f08f3c1717b4688a5cc9704c9527092dd16761cd9b19"} {"question" "q-79373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-79373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{2})"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{4}-x+2}{2})"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2x-2)"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x)"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-79373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x}=3$ that satisfies $y(0)=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x} & =3 \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3+2x{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{e}^{-x}+2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{e}^{-x}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-3{e}^{-x}+{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=-3$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-3 \\\\ -3{e}^{-0}+{0}^{2}+C & =-3 \\\\ C-3 & =-3 \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x}=3$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-3$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "419bff3195711dba4c75f08f3c1717b4688a5cc9704c9527092dd16761cd9b19"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2{e}^{-x}-1"] ["math" "y=4x+{e}^{-3x}-4"] ["math" "y=x+{e}^{-3x}-4"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}+2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(-1)=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{1}{x}+x+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(-1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{1-(-1)^{2}-C(-1)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{C} & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "419bff3195711dba4c75f08f3c1717b4688a5cc9704c9527092dd16761cd9b19"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\frac{x}{1+x+{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{2+2x-{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{2x+{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-2x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ C-1 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "419bff3195711dba4c75f08f3c1717b4688a5cc9704c9527092dd16761cd9b19"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(\\frac{5}{4}-e^{-x})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "558730831d044e038a30029b5e67d3c113f4bceb2749c467df2169a795923843"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =5x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm {e}^{5x+C} \\\\  & =\\pm {e}^{C}{e}^{5x} \\\\  & =K{e}^{5x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3 \\\\ K{e}^{5\\cdot 0} & =3 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x}  \\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that  $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0.$ Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "edc09ff35a24b70d6c2638ee48f556632b26068878c35e77203253786ae1d2a3"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C.$\n\nNow let's apply the condition $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$ to find $C_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =0+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)   =  \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "edc09ff35a24b70d6c2638ee48f556632b26068878c35e77203253786ae1d2a3"}] "usage" {"q-104055" [] "e-541" [] "q-104059" [] "q-355528" [] "q-79371" [] "q-355577" [] "e-540" []} "basis" 1514 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186290335 17592186290336 17592186290337 17592186290338 17592186290339 17592186290356 17592186290366 17592186292417 17592186292418 17592186292419 17592186292420 17592186292421 17592186296410 17592186296411 175921